  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The two best experiments (config_034: 0.715, config_008: 0.721) both use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, showing that the RNA encoder choice is the dominant factor. However, we have no RNA-only baseline with scvi_n200 + multiprofile, so we cannot determine whether the image modality is actually contributing meaningful complementary information or whether the high performance is driven entirely by the RNA encoder. With scgpt, the image added only ~0.02 over RNA-alone (0.411 vs 0.435), suggesting the image contribution may be marginal. Config_025 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_034 (removing the image). If RNA alone approaches ~0.70, the image is not adding value and we can simplify the pipeline; if it drops to ~0.50–0.60, the image is providing substantial complementary signal and further image-encoder or fusion experiments become high-priority. Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental modality-contribution question is more informative than a small fusion-method tweak (e.g., weighted vs concat) that is unlikely to change the ranking of top configurations."
}

